<title>UK: NatWest, Barclays up on buyback talk.</title>
<headline>NatWest, Barclays up on buyback talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in NatWest Bank and Barclays rose, even as the broad market slid, as renewed talk about share buybacks sparked what dealers called a technical squeeze.</p>
<p>By 1131 GMT, NatWest shares were up 8p to 733-1/2 while shares in Barclays climbed 10-1/2p to 1038-1/2, and looked set to test their all-time high of 1042p.</p>
</text>
